text:
Verification checklist
ip -br a
ip route
ip -6 route
ip route get &lt;dst&gt;
ping -c 2 &lt;dst&gt;
ping -6 -c 2 &lt;dst6&gt;

Asymmetric routing
Forward path R1→R2→R3, return R3→R4→R1. Stateless ping may work; stateful firewalls and some reverse-path filters break.
Always verify both directions.
# from each side
ping -c 2 &lt;other&gt;
traceroute -n &lt;other&gt;

IPv6 notes
IPv6 routers do not fragment in the same way; PMTUD is even more critical. Minimum link MTU is 1280.
ping -6 -M do -s 1400 &lt;dst&gt;
ip -6 route get &lt;dst&gt;
